        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "64668af2-36be-594c-a708-4b7137faf969",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Munich, Germany, Netherlands\n- Organizations: Bürgerbräukeller, Löwenbräu, Anheuser-Busch InBev, German Nazi government\n- People: Georg Elser, Adolf Hitler\n- Events: Venlo Incident, failed assassination attempt, invasion of the Netherlands\n\nFacts:\n- The Bürgerbräukeller was a large beer hall in Munich, Germany.\n- Löwenbräu is a brewery in Munich that is owned by Anheuser-Busch InBev.\n- On 8 November 1939, Georg Elser carried out a failed assassination attempt on German Chancellor Adolf Hitler at the Bürgerbräukeller in Munich, Germany.\n- The German Nazi government later used the Venlo Incident to link Britain to Georg Elser's failed assassination attempt.\n- The German Nazi government used the Venlo Incident to help justify Germany's invasion of the neutral Netherlands on 10 May 1940.",
